9. (a) In order to discharge the onus of proving issues put upon it, plaintiff firm examined its Authorized Representative Shri Anshul Bansal as PW-1 in the matter,
who in his evidence by way of Affidavit Ex.PW1/A has reiterated the averments made in the plaint and referred to the following documents:
(i) Duly attested copy of Registration Certificate [Form GST REG-06] in respect of the plaintiff firm namely M/s Balaji Trading Co., as Ex.PW1/1;
(ii) True copy of Authority Letter dated 19.04.2024, executed by plaintiff firm in favour of PW-1 as Ex.PW1/2 (OSR);
(iii) True copy of the ledger account maintained by the plaintiff firm in respect of the transactions done with the defendant for the period from 01.04.2022 to 31.03.2023,
wherein a sum of Rs.4,62,880/- is being shown as "Debit Balance" as on 21.04.2022 as Ex.PW1/3;
(iv) True copy(ies) of Invoice bearing No.10362, dated 15.03.2022, for Rs.79,000/-;
Invoice No.10510, dated 19.03.2022, for Rs.79,000/-; Invoice No.36, dated 01.04.2022, for Rs.96,250/-;
Invoice No.48, dated 02.04.2022, for Rs.57,750/-; Invoice No.236, dated 06.04.2022, for Rs.1,13,500/-; and Invoice No.300, dated 08.04.2022, for Rs.77,000/-; as Ex.PW1/4 (Colly);
CS (Comm) No.779/2024: M/s Balaji Trading Company V/s M/s Puneet Retails: DOD: 04.09.2025 (v) Two original cheques bearing Nos.003255, dated 14.04.2022 for Rs.1,00,000/- and cheque No.003256, dated 16.04.2022, for Rs.1,15,752/-, both drawn on ICICI Bank Limited as Ex.PW1/5;
(vi) True copy of legal notice dated 16.09.2024, sent on behalf of plaintiff to the defendant as Ex.PW1/6;
(vii) Original Tracking Receipt and Internet downloaded tracking report as Ex.PW1/7;
(viii) Certificate of Non-Starter Report dated 22.11.2024, issued under the signatures of Secretary,
DLSA, North-West as Ex.PW1/8;
